good Eve  and welcome to the 8th annual Academy of  Motion Picture Arts and Sciences  governor's Awards tonight is an  opportunity to remind us what we love  about movies not just the fact that they  can entertain and enlighten us but how  in uncertain times they can connect us  change us and unify us  and tonight is our opportunity to honor  those whose careers have transformed our  industry and set new standards of  excellence we honor them for they have  touched us beyond measure but we do so  knowing that one day they will hand the  baton to other remarkable talents some  of whom have not yet even been born at  the academy we are committed to  empowering that next generation of  creative talent and ensuring that next  generation represents the real face of  America and the world and that is why  inclusion isn't just a favor we're doing  for anyone it's a strategic imperative  for our industry  despite what the press may tell you it  isn't about a magical algorithm typed  into a search engine it is names not  just numbers substance not justice  statistics bringing new voices and new  faces into the room and making sure they  are heard and seen and it's about change  top to bottom and that change is  underway and thanks to your hard work  and support the progress we have made is  being noticed around the world but even  with all that has been accomplished  that's not enough for us we're not to  the mountaintop yet but we can see the  peak up ahead we can't get there without  you so I ask you tonight to help us  chart that new course to find talent and  lift it up to higher to recruit to  mentor and never ever to give up on the  promise of taking a shot on the new kid  the way someone took a shot with you to  that end  to that end the Academy brought together  the cornerstones of our industry studios  distributors guilds production companies  all of you in this room to launch the  Academy's talent development and  inclusion program which will create  paths and opportunities for students  into our industry and with our doing  that we will reflect the face of the  world and the audiences we hope to share  our art with all over this planet ask  any writer any director any actor and  they'll tell you that the heart of  moviemaking is all about perspective  whose point of view is being represented  what do you see through the camera lens  who is behind the camera itself imagine  the difference it will make when we open  our industry to reflect the complete  mosaic and diversity of our world of our  world the movements and conversations it  can trigger and that's our mission  to find the next Jackie Chan the next  envy coats the next Lin stall master and  the nets Frederick Wiseman  what an amazing standard tonight's  honorees have already set for our  industry you'll hear much more about  each of their individual accomplishments  throughout the evening but for now let  me say this about what tonight's  honorees have in common they inspire the  next generation with the same sense of  wonder and enchantment that first  touched all of us as kids they lift up  so many each time they share with the  world through the power of film new ways  of looking at our world and they believe  that art creativity conscience  conviction telling your story and  knowing that someone somewhere will see  their own reflection in your vision that  remains as powerful as it was a hundred  years ago when the first film was made  in California and so a toast to our  honorees jackie and lynn frederick on  behalf of the Board of Governors and the  entire Academy congratulations  Cheers
 

